WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.340
Warner Brothers dropped the first teaser trailer
for director Todd Phillips' Joker movie on

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:09.720
Wednesday, April 3rd, and the internet went
nuts as fans sparked a fiery debate over which

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:13.889
actor might be the better Joker: The Dark
Knight's Heath Ledger or the brand-new Clown

00:00:13.889 --> 00:00:16.230
Prince of Crime, Joaquin Phoenix.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:19.180
When it comes to The Joker, everyone has their
favorite version.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:24.010
Some prefer Cesar Romero's portrayal of the
character on the 1960s Batman television series.

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:29.410
"And I can start planning the craftiest caper
of my career!"

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:33.870
Others think the 1980s brought the best-ever
interpretation of Mr. J by Jack Nicholson,

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:36.620
who played the Joker in Tim Burton's Batman
film.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.140
"Do I look like I'm joking?"

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:44.180
A fair few out there are a little more radical,
preferring Jared Leto's silver-toothed, tattooed

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:46.360
take on the Joker in Suicide Squad.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.120
"Bring the car around.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.860
We're going for a drive."

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.640
And some people think the live-action versions
of the infamous character pale in comparison

00:00:56.649 --> 00:00:58.660
to Mark Hamill's voiceover work.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:02.260
"Hahahaha, let the good times roll."

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:06.609
But it's the late Heath Ledger who probably
captivates audiences the most.

00:01:06.609 --> 00:01:09.630
"Why so serious?"

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:13.659
To this day, many fans still believe no one
can even come close to his stunning turn as

00:01:13.659 --> 00:01:16.090
the Joker in Christopher Nolan's The Dark
Knight.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:20.950
However, now there's a new Joker in town:
Joaquin Phoenix's Arthur Fleck, the aspiring

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:25.159
comedian who experiences a psychotic break
and becomes the Joker.

00:01:25.159 --> 00:01:29.029
Unsurprisingly, social media and numerous
entertainment sites have been weighing in

00:01:29.029 --> 00:01:32.060
on which actor may end up reigning the best
Joker.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:36.359
Shortly after watching the footage of director
Todd Phillips' Joker, one fan took to Twitter

00:01:36.359 --> 00:01:40.209
to say that Phoenix will be "the best Joker
we've ever seen."

00:01:40.209 --> 00:01:45.009
Another fan wrote that Phoenix is "coming
for Heath Ledger's crown as the best Joker."

00:01:45.009 --> 00:01:48.579
One Twitter user was so blown away by seeing
Phoenix in character that they placed an early

00:01:48.579 --> 00:01:50.200
bet on the outcome of the film:

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.829
"Calling it now, Joaquin Phoenix is going
to be the best live action Joker."

00:01:54.829 --> 00:01:58.710
Many fans were quick to bring up Ledger's
performance for direct comparison, with one

00:01:58.710 --> 00:01:59.779
Twitter user writing:

00:01:59.779 --> 00:02:04.349
"I have a great feeling that Joaquin Phoenix's
Joker is gonna better than Heath Ledger's"

00:02:04.349 --> 00:02:08.899
Jemele Hill, a staff writer for The Atlantic,
feels like Phoenix might end up turning in

00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:09.899
a better performance:

00:02:09.899 --> 00:02:13.629
"I didn't think it was possible for anyone
to play the Joker better than Heath Ledger.

00:02:13.629 --> 00:02:15.620
But Joaquin Phoenix looks like he's got a
shot."

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:20.940
Tia Fabi of Geek Vibes Nation wrote an opinion
piece about why Phoenix will probably go down

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.560
as one of the best Jokers in history, writing
in part:

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:33.880
Meanwhile, one fan was evidently prepared
to turn the online debate into a real-life

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:34.500
battle:

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.480
"Heath Ledger will never be replaced as the
best Joker.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:38.400
Fight me."

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.659
Writer George M. Johnson wrote that people
should, quote, "let the Joker rest with the

00:02:42.659 --> 00:02:43.680
best that did it."

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:47.700
That's clearly a reference to Ledger, who
passed away in 2008 at the age of 28.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.920
Advocate April Reign later responded to Johnson's
tweet, writing:

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.290
"This is my thought as well.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:55.980
Why anyone would even ATTEMPT this after Heath
is beyond me."

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:00.599
Clearly passionate about all things Joker,
professional Fortnite player Nate Hill tweeted:

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:03.960
"Heath Ledger's Joker was so good the character
should be retired...

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:07.320
I will compare every Joker to Heath and they
always will fall short."

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.620
The debate was just as hardcore over Instagram.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.840
One individual wrote that Ledger is the best
Joker, and that, quote,

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:16.160
Another argued:

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:25.860
Some fans simply refused to choose a favorite
Joker and instead argued that comparisons

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:29.749
simply can't be made, as the actors appear
to be playing different iterations of the

00:03:29.749 --> 00:03:30.830
classic character.

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:34.469
"Joaquin is portraying the early developments
of the Joker character…

00:03:34.469 --> 00:03:37.230
Heath Ledger is the developed character in
the years following.

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:39.209
It'd be silly to compare the two."

00:03:39.209 --> 00:03:42.450
Another fan basically asked the Internet to
stop being the Internet:

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:45.600
"Can we stop comparing, 'Who did this character
best?'

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:46.280
Please?

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:49.800
Ugh, online fandom is just taking the fun
out of everything I swear."

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.300
One Twitter user actually made a good point:

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.520
"Heath Ledger and Joaquin Phoenix were friends.

00:03:54.529 --> 00:03:58.510
So, how about we stop with the extreme comparisons
of their Joker performances...

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:00.360
It's disrespectful and tasteless."

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:04.029
It goes without saying that these are just
a few selections out of the thousands of responses

00:04:04.029 --> 00:04:08.109
fans posted after seeing the Joker teaser,
and opinions are bound to change as the film

00:04:08.109 --> 00:04:11.719
nears its release date, and after we all finally
get to watch the thing.

00:04:11.719 --> 00:04:15.519
Whether you're a fan of Phoenix, a longtime
Ledger-lover, or someone who still doesn't

00:04:15.519 --> 00:04:19.650
want to pick sides, try to keep an open mind
about Joker… and try not to get into any

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:20.860
social media fights.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:26.340
Joker will tumble into theaters on October
4th, 2019.

